      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer. According to [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never loading it into that environment at all.** Instead:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected **only into the environment of spawned child processes** (the Ingest agent or Query agent) immediately before those processes start\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n\nThis design means a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only in the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API. The same scoping model applies to both the Ingest agent and Query agent processes.",
